"closed_at":"2026-05-19T16:22:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.stable, 4.6.stable, 4.6.2.stable, 4.7-beta2\n- Not Reproducible in: 4.0.stable, 4.1.stable, 4.2.stable, 4.3.stable, 4.4.stable, 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nCachyOs - Godot 4.6.2-stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nSome JPEG Images that Imports/loads just fine pre 4.5, fails on later versions of Godot. \nLooking through the 4.5 Changelog I suspect its and issue with the switch to libjpeg-turbo https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104347, but I'm no expert so I could be wrong \n\n<img width=\"537\" height=\"308\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f81e8c9d-850a-4a25-9f11-cc20e909ed86\" />\n\nFurthermore these images displays fine in Krita, Gimp, Gwenview and Librewolf browser, so even if these images have some quirks they should clearly still be usable.\n\nI hope some of you smart people can solve this regression <3   \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSimply drag the folder of JPEG Images into the FileSystem Dock\n\n[some failed to import jpeg's.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27905589/some.failed.to.import.jpeg.s.zip)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[4.4.1-jpeg-images-does-import-.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27905579/4.4.1-jpeg-images-does-import-.zip)\n\n[4.6.2-jpeg-images-does-not-import.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27905582/4.6.2-jpeg-images-does-not-import.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repit